# Android / Gradle
*.iml
.gradle/
local.properties
build/
captures/
.externalNativeBuild/
.cxx/

# IDE
.idea/

# Keys and secrets
*.jks
*.keystore

# Big or generated
*.apk
*.aab
*.bin
*.onnx
*.zip
models/

# ⚠⚠ ...but a TEST FIXTURE is not a model archive. These are kilobytes, and one
# of them cannot be synthesised by the suite even in principle: it reproduces a
# bug in another tool's zip WRITER (PowerShell's Compress-Archive emits `\`
# separators), and every zip built with ZipOutputStream is conformant. Ignoring
# it would leave a green suite on a clean clone with the regression unguarded.
!app/src/test/resources/*.zip

# ⚠ The forked C++ backend is NC-licensed and must never be published.
# Mirror edits into backend-patches/ instead -- that patch is the only record.
backend-src/

# Personal Claude Code config -- references the private ../LocalDream tree
.claude/settings.local.json

# Personal launcher -- profile switching + skip-permissions, not project material
claude-yolo.bat

# Stray device captures. Screenshots go to the scratchpad, never the repo --
# they routinely contain whatever the user had on screen.
/shot.png
/*-shot.png
/screenshots/

# Kotlin compiler scratch. Contains absolute paths and is pure build noise.
.kotlin/

# ⚠⚠ NEVER COMMIT THESE. Both are redistribution hazards, not just big files:
#   - libstable_diffusion_core.so is built from backend-src/, which descends
#     from CC BY-NC `local-dream`.
#   - the QNN runtime libs come from the QAIRT SDK, which has its own
#     redistribution restrictions.
# They are BUILD OUTPUT staged into the app by tools/stage_backend.ps1, and the
# app is useless without them -- which is exactly why the temptation to commit
# them will recur. Don't.
app/src/main/jniLibs/
app/src/main/assets/qnnlibs/
app/src/main/assets/ditlibs/

# QuickJS is fetched, not vendored -- tools/fetch_quickjs.ps1 (pinned tag + sha256).
# Our CMakeLists and JNI bridge beside it ARE committed.
app/src/main/cpp/third_party/

# ⚠ The QNN headers libnmqnn.so is built against -- QAIRT SDK material with its
# own redistribution terms, fetched by tools/fetch_qnn_headers.ps1. `nmqnn.cpp`
# and the CMakeLists beside them ARE committed.
app/src/main/cpp/include/

# ⚠ The NPU canary (tools/stage_neodragon.ps1). Build output of ../Neodragon's
# conversion pipeline, and a `.bin` the rule above would catch anyway -- named
# here so the reason is recorded rather than inferred.
app/src/main/assets/npu/

# Dev docs stay out of the published tree (the user's call, 2026-09-10). The
# ones already in history are left alone; nothing NEW is added.
docs/DEVICES.md

# ⚠⚠ DOCS AND NOTES ARE LOCAL ONLY (the user's call, 2026-09-10).
#
# Everything in docs/ and notes/, CLAUDE.md, and backend-patches/README.md are
# working material: measurements, wrong turns, device serials in prose, and the
# reasoning behind decisions that have since changed. They are what makes the
# next session cheap and they are not what a reader of a public repo wants.
#
# ⚠ The root README.md is the ONE exception and is negated below. It is the
# canonical description of the project; if something matters to an outsider it
# belongs there, not in a doc that is no longer published.
#
# ⚠⚠ These files still exist on disk and are still the source of truth for
# working on this. "Not in the repo" is not "deleted".
*.md
# The ROOT readme only. A bare `!README.md` would also un-ignore
# backend-patches/README.md, which is working material like the rest.
!/README.md

# ⚠ The icon SOURCE artwork. `tools/build_icon.py` generates every asset under
# res/mipmap-* from it, and those are committed; shipping the source too invites
# someone to edit it and wonder why nothing changed.
icon-source.png

# ⚠ The raw screen captures. `media/workflows.png` is the committed one; the
# video it was cut from is three times the size for no benefit in a README.
media/*.mp4
media/*.gif
